Installation smoke test
=======================

After the build in `INSTALL`, run:

    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

CTest runs `sdpasolve` on `examples/truss1.dat-s` and checks both the process
exit code and the solver's `SDP Status: Primal dual optimal` output. Both are
needed: an unsupported input type can currently exit with status zero while
printing an error message.

To test the installed executable, run:

    cmake -DSOLVER="$PWD/install/bin/sdpasolve" \
          -DINSTANCE="$PWD/examples/truss1.dat-s" \
          -P tests/check_sdpasolve.cmake

To add a small regression instance later, put its input under `examples/`,
register another `add_test` in `CMakeLists.txt`, and use the checker script to
assert its expected status. For numerical regressions, extend the checker to
compare a documented objective value and tolerance as well.
